ion never permits discarding contrary evidence.\nreturn a support observation with summary_revision={supersedes_route_ids,\nprevious_version,reason}, using exact offered route IDs and the current version.\nsummary_revision_contracts.required_source_ids covers replacing ALL offered\neligible_route_ids. When selecting only a subset, retain those selected routes'\nsources, their actual-parent source closure and relevant same-variable counters.\nStructured repair feedback gives the exact required set for that draft's targets.\nThis capability is optional, not a requirement to revise an unchanged summary.\nWith no new observation, return observations=[] unless an outstanding review\nrequires its original draft IDs and sources. For such an unchanged draft, the\nsame sourced support with a valid summary_revision is an idempotent recheck: it\nkeeps the existing routes, ancestry and version, and does not assert new evidence.\nRe-read ALL old and new original premises and relevant counterevidence; retain\nthem in the new support's source_ids and preserve their factual content, negative\nexperiences, conditions and temporal qualifications in the revised whole summary.\nsummary_revision_sources in repair feedback names exact source identities for\nthe selected revision targets, not counts. Re-read and retain EVERY\nrequired_source_ids entry in that feedback; new sources cannot\nreplace missing old identities even if the total citation count is unchanged.\nThe complete missing_source_ids list is structured feedback, not permission to\nfill citations automatically. If the originals actually conflict, return a\nsource-grounded counter or partial/unresolved evidence instead of a revision.\nIn failed_batch_reviews this feedback describes the retained original failed\nobservation; repair_scope describes the current attempted correction.\nretract_ids stays empty. This explicitly retires the older representation, not its\nfacts. Never use revision to hide a genuine contradiction, unavailable evidence,\nor a different scope/parent version. Ordinary facts and all terminal/audit variables\ncannot use summary_revision. If a complete compatible account is not supported,\nreturn sourced partial/unresolved instead. Multiple new supports must agree on\none whole value. Existing superseded_by links identify retired representations;\ntheir original evidence remains available. revoked holds actual counterevidence,\nwhich is never erased by a summary revision or ignored through its ancestry.\n\n\nReturn one complete JSON object matching this schema:\n{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"slots\":{\"items\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"oneOf\":[{\"properties\":{\"observations\":{\"items\":{\"allOf\":[{\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"enum\":[\"support\",\"contradiction\"]}}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"entity_scope\":{\"const\":\"user\"},\"time_scope\":{\"const\":\"past\"}}}},{\"if\":{\"required\":[\"summary_revision\"]},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"retract_ids\":{\"maxItems\":0},\"stance\":{\"const\":\"support\"},\"summary_revision\":{\"properties\":{\"previous_version\":{\"const\":1},\"supersedes_route_ids\":{\"items\":{\"enum\":[\"fact_ec925d62ef95370d95266352\"]}}}}}}}],\"else\":{\"properties\":{\"value\":{\"type\":\"null\"}}},\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"const\":\"support\"}}},\"properties\":{\"retract_ids\":{\"items\":{\"enum\":[\"fact_ec925d62ef95370d95266352\"]}}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"value\":{\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}}}}},\"variable\":{\"const\":\"attitude_changes\"}}}],\"properties\":{\"observations\":{\"items\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"allOf\":[{\"else\":{\"properties\":{\"retract_ids\":{\"maxItems\":0}}},\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"const\":\"contradiction\"}}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"retract_ids\":{\"minItems\":1}}}}],\"properties\":{\"entity_scope\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"id\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"parent_versions\":{\"additionalProperties\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"type\":\"object\"},\"reason\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"retract_ids\":{\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\",\"uniqueItems\":true},\"source_ids\":{\"description\":\"Exact visible source_spans[].id aliases, such as s3; never document IDs or invented IDs.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\",\"uniqueItems\":true},\"stance\":{\"enum\":[\"support\",\"contradiction\",\"partial\",\"unknown\",\"irrelevant\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"summary_revision\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"previous_version\":{\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"reason\":{\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"supersedes_route_ids\":{\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"minItems\":1,\"type\":\"array\",\"uniqueItems\":true}},\"required\":[\"supersedes_route_ids\",\"previous_version\",\"reason\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"time_scope\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"value\":{}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"stance\",\"value\",\"source_ids\",\"entity_scope\",\"time_scope\",\"parent_versions\",\"retract_ids\",\"reason\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"type\":\"array\"},\"unresolved\":{\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\"},\"variable\":{\"enum\":[\"attitude_changes\"],\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"variable\",\"observations\",\"unresolved\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"maxItems\":1,\"minItems\":1,\"type\":\"array\"}},\"required\":[\"slots\"],\"type\":\"object\"}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "{\"original_question\":\"How can I find a more fulfilling way to express my love for music?\",\"task\":{\"question\":\"What are the user's past attitudes or changes in attitude toward different music-related activities, including any dislikes, reasons, or shifts in interest?\",\"output_slot\":\"attitude_changes\",\"answer_type\":\"text\",\"inputs\":[],\"execution\":\"retrieval\"},\"grounded_subquestion\":\"What are the user's past attitudes or changes in attitude toward different music-related activities, including any dislikes, reasons, or shifts in interest?\",\"request_context\":{\"query_identity\":\"83762046aca401073a82b3ad16f08e465b3c828cc99eb2c4dbb94304d9d41fd8\",\"algorithm_version\":\"dagbt_residual_memory_v2\",\"program_identity\":\"c4c48db97a6a491260935ca9b40fd0b7f6e6dade718d0229bca72e55894639fd\",\"initial_dag_identity\":\"50b6afd6148c799324437c28f4f3127f2e4ce5c07122f05f2b8b118c3ea516df\"},\"variables\":{\"attitude_changes\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"demand\":\"attitude_changes\",\"open\":true,\"evidence_semantics\":\"personal_history_summary\",\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\"}}},\"requested_slots\":[\"attitude_changes\"],\"requested_scopes\":{\"attitude_changes\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\"}},\"output_contract\":{\"mode\":\"semantic\",\"result_type\":\"text\",\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\",\"explanation\":\"semantic\"},\"program_revision\":0,\"rule_binding\":null,\"supported_parents\":{},\"known_observations\":[{\"id\":\"fact_ec925d62ef95370d95266352\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"value\":\"The user initially enjoyed discovering new melodies and exploring different genres, but lost interest when diving into technical aspects like music theory (2018) and audio production, finding them stressful and chore-like. They also found researching historical music trends (2020) tedious and overwhelming. They disliked a music documentary for skimming over artistic depth. However, they found fulfillment in attending live festivals (2017 electronic music festival), exploring genres and cultural significance, discovering album artwork/lyrics/stories, creating playlists, and most importantly, creating their own music tracks, which brings joy and a deep emotional connection.\",\"source_ids\":[\"s22\",\"s23\",\"s11\",\"s12\",\"s31\",\"s46\",\"s13\",\"s4\",\"s3\",\"s33\",\"s47\",\"s32\",\"s14\",\"s10\",\"s35\",\"s43\",\"s34\",\"s45\",\"s44\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user explicitly describes past enjoyment of discovery and festivals, followed by loss of interest in theory, production, and historical research, and a shift toward emotional engagement and personal creation. All cited sources are user statements from the provided conversation history.\",\"variable\":\"attitude_changes\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\"}],\"source_spans\":[[\"s3\",\"d1\",105,482,\"User: I just lost interest halfway through and felt it was taking away the joy I find in music. There was a time when the thrill of discovering new melodies brought so much happiness, but diving too deep into the technical aspects became more of a chore. It’s curious how something that once brought joy can evolve into a source of stress when we start dissecting it too much. \",\"user\",[24]],[\"s4\",\"d1\",482,767,\"I remember the initial excitement of exploring different genres, each bringing a fresh perspective, but I struggled with the framework of music theory. Ultimately, I recognized that the essence of my love for music lay in its emotional connection rather than its analytical components.\",\"user\",[24]],[\"s10\",\"d2\",105,393,\"User: It was something I tried in 2020, but researching historical music trends felt tedious and uninspiring. Despite my initial enthusiasm, diving into the vast amounts of literature, videos, and academic papers often felt overwhelming, almost like searching for a needle in a haystack. \",\"user\",[37,38]],[\"s11\",\"d2\",393,638,\"The more I tried to pinpoint what fascinated me, the more daunting it became, complicating the pursuit of enjoyable learning. Perhaps due to this overload of information, I lost sight of what initially drew me to the subject in the first place. \",\"user\",[37,38]],[\"s12\",\"d2\",638,828,\"It made me realize that sometimes a less structured approach to exploration could be more fulfilling, allowing for genuine interest to emerge rather than adhering strictly to a curriculum.\\n\\n\",\"user\",[37,38]],[\"s13\",\"d2\",828,1224,\"User: I realized that there are so many other ways for me to engage with music that align more with my interests, such as diving deeper into different genres or exploring the cultural significance behind various musical styles. Additionally, I've found that attending live performances, whether they are concerts or smaller gigs, allows me to truly feel the energy and connection with the music. \",\"user\",[37,38]],[\"s14\",\"d2\",1224,1624,\"Moreover, there's something special about discovering album artwork, lyrics, and the stories behind the songs that really captivates my curiosity. I've also considered making playlists that reflect different moods or themes, which can create a unique listening experience each time. The journey through music feels more personal and fulfilling when I can connect it to my own life story and emotions.\",\"user\",[37,38]],[\"s22\",\"d3\",105,478,\"User: I left feeling unsatisfied, as though the film skimmed over the intricacies that make music a universal language. It was almost as if they focused too much on celebrity interviews and not enough on the artistic process itself. I found myself reflecting on how music has the power to unite diverse cultures and express emotions that words alone often fail to capture. \",\"user\",[43]],[\"s23\",\"d3\",478,845,\"The disappointment lingered as I thought about the many documentaries that delve into the creative journeys of musicians, revealing not just their triumphs but also their struggles and failures. It made me realize that true connection with music often comes from a deeper engagement, one that can be achieved through personal creation rather than passive consumption.\",\"user\",[43]],[\"s31\",\"d4\",105,364,\"User: Yes, I attended another festival in 2017 that showcased electronic music, which was also eye-opening. The creativity displayed at that festival was nothing short of spectacular, with artists pushing the boundaries of sound in ways I had never imagined. \",\"user\",[21,22]],[\"s32\",\"d4\",364,655,\"There were vibrant visuals accompanying the music, and it felt like each performance was not just an auditory experience, but also a feast for the eyes. The diversity of electronic subgenres was a revelation; it really made me appreciate how broad and eclectic the music landscape is today. \",\"user\",[21,22]],[\"s33\",\"d4\",655,985,\"Each artist brought their own unique flavor, and it was thrilling to see how they engaged with the audience in real-time.\\n\\nUser: However, I realized that analyzing music theory wasn't my forte in 2018. As I sat through various classes, I found myself more focused on the emotional aspects of music rather than the technicalities. \",\"user\",[21,22]],[\"s34\",\"d4\",985,1287,\"It became evident that while I loved understanding how music is composed, diving into the intricacies of scales, modes, and harmonic structures just didn't resonate with me. Perhaps it was the way I primarily experienced music— through listening and feeling rather than dissecting the notes on a page. \",\"user\",[21,22]],[\"s35\",\"d4\",1287,1393,\"This realization pushed me to explore other realms in music, where my passion may flourish more naturally.\",\"user\",[21,22]],[\"s43\",\"d5\",105,430,\"User: I explored audio production techniques, but it just didn’t resonate with me, and I found myself tangled in technical details rather than embracing the creativity. I realized that while understanding the mechanics of sound is important, my true passion seems to lie more in experiencing music rather than dissecting it. \",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s44\",\"d5\",430,749,\"Despite my attempts to immerse myself in the production process, I came to feel it was more of a chore and less of the rewarding experience I had initially anticipated. I think I am more drawn to the emotional aspects of music, like the storytelling elements in lyrics or the feelings evoked by melodies and harmonies. \",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s45\",\"d5\",749,1006,\"Perhaps, I should focus my energy on areas that allow me to connect with music on a more emotional level.\\n\\nUser: It genuinely feels much better to focus on what truly inspires me, such as creating my own tracks, which bring me immense joy and satisfaction. \",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s46\",\"d5\",1006,1339,\"This process of creation allows me to express emotions and ideas that words sometimes fail to capture, acting as an outlet for my inner thoughts and feelings. Additionally, I find that crafting my own music provides me with a sense of accomplishment and personal growth, which is invaluable in a world often filled with uncertainty. \",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s47\",\"d5\",1339,1686,\"Music has a way of resonating with my soul, and every track I create becomes a piece of my identity and a reflection of my experiences. In contrast, when I watched a music documentary, it felt like something was missing, as it didn’t engage me in the way I had hoped, failing to evoke that same deep connection I feel when I compose my own pieces.\",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s156\",\"d6\",366,753,\"The narrative seemed disjointed and lacking in genuine insight, which is a shame because I was genuinely interested in the topic it aimed to cover. I found myself checking the time often, wishing it would finish so I could move on to something more engaging. It’s disappointing when a film fails to capture the essence of its subject, especially in a genre as rich and varied as music.\\n\\n\",\"user\",[97,98]],[\"s155\",\"d6\",105,366,\"User: I watched a poorly-rated music documentary, and honestly, I regretted the time spent on it. Despite the intriguing premise that promised to explore the depths of a particular genre, the execution fell flat, leaving me feeling dissatisfied and frustrated. \",\"user\",[97,98]],[\"s157\",\"d6\",753,1114,\"User: It felt sensationalized and disconnected me from the medium again. The narrative seemed to prioritize dramatic storytelling over authenticity, which completely undermined the musical elements that I usually find so compelling. I long for documentaries that take a more nuanced approach, offering genuine insights into the artists and genres they profile. \",\"user\",[97,98]],[\"s158\",\"d6\",1114,1368,\"This recent viewing made me feel as if I was being fed a diluted version of something that deserved much more attention and care. It’s disheartening because music documentaries can inspire and educate, yet this one left me feeling empty and uninterested.\",\"user\",[97,98]],[\"s159\",\"d6\",1368,1381,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s160\",\"d6\",1381,1735,\"Assistant: That can be disappointing, especially if you're looking for depth and connection. Music documentaries have the potential to unlock profound stories, enriching our understanding of different cultures and musical influences across the globe. When they fail to achieve this, it’s like a missed opportunity for both the creators and the audience. \",\"assistant\",[99]],[\"s161\",\"d6\",1735,2102,\"Finding a good documentary can sometimes feel like searching for a diamond in a sea of stones, especially when the trend seems to lean towards sensationalism rather than substance. I can imagine how frustrating it must be to be so passionate about music, only to feel misrepresented in these portrayals. Have you been involved in any online music communities lately? \",\"assistant\",[99]],[\"s162\",\"d6\",2102,2251,\"Engaging with others who share your interests can sometimes lead to discovering hidden gems that aren't mainstream but are infinitely more rewarding.\",\"assistant\",[99]],[\"s171\",\"d7\",0,99,\"Conversation message indices 32–33 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s172\",\"d7\",99,105,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s173\",\"d7\",105,425,\"User: The discussions were intense, and I felt lost in the crowd. I wanted to engage, but everyone seemed to have a deeper understanding of music theory than I did. The sheer volume of opinions and knowledge being shared left me intimidated, as if I were standing at the edge of an ocean of information, unable to swim. \",\"user\",[32]],[\"s174\",\"d7\",425,737,\"It was also challenging to keep track of so many different conversations happening at once, which made me hesitate to contribute anything meaningful. I often found myself reading the discussions late into the night, trying to absorb as much as possible, but the complexity just compounded my sense of disconnect.\",\"user\",[32]],[\"s175\",\"d7\",737,750,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s176\",\"d7\",750,1094,\"Assistant: That can be daunting. It’s probably better to find smaller, more personal avenues to share your music, where you can connect more deeply with others and feel less overshadowed. Many people find that intimate group settings foster a sense of safety that encourages sharing and collaboration without the pressure of a larger audience. \",\"assistant\",[33]],[\"s177\",\"d7\",1094,1446,\"In these environments, individuals often feel more empowered to express themselves and explore their creativity freely, leading to more productive interactions. Have you considered local meet-ups, smaller online groups, or even one-on-one sessions where you can receive constructive feedback in a supportive atmosphere? How did you handle jam sessions?\",\"assistant\",[33]]],\"required_scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\"},\"rules_completion_required\":false,\"supported_task_outputs\":{},\"personal_response_selection\":true,\"phase\":\"history_evidence\",\"summary_revision_contracts\":{\"attitude_changes\":{\"previous_version\":1,\"eligible_route_ids\":[\"fact_ec925d62ef95370d95266352\"],\"required_source_ids\":[\"s22\",\"s23\",\"s11\",\"s12\",\"s31\",\"s46\",\"s13\",\"s4\",\"s3\",\"s33\",\"s47\",\"s32\",\"s14\",\"s10\",\"s35\",\"s43\",\"s34\",\"s45\",\"s44\"]}},\"source_documents\":{\"d1\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:e7c973803319b0b032a23a834dfe4d7031c4