:\"The user has explored various genres and attended festivals, including an electronic music festival in 2017. They tried music theory classes in 2018 but found it unfulfilling, preferring emotional connection over technical analysis. They attempted audio production techniques but found it a chore. They have created their own tracks, which brings joy and satisfaction. They also watched a music documentary that felt unsatisfying. They have not played an instrument, sung, or composed in a formal sense, but they create original tracks as a personal creative outlet. Additionally, they have blended nature sounds into their music, taught young musicians, explored their cultural heritage through music, developed an app blending traditional and modern sounds, studied Pacific music theory, collaborated with other musicians, and watched documentaries on cultural music evolution. They also faced criticism in music reviewing, leading to a more personal expression focus.\",\"t1\":\"The user prefers an emotional, personal, and creative engagement with music over technical or analytical approaches. They enjoy attending live performances (festivals, concerts, smaller gigs), exploring genres and cultural significance, discovering album artwork, lyrics, and stories behind songs, making mood-based playlists, and creating their own tracks. They dislike music theory, audio production, and historical research as they find these tedious and stressful. They have limited time or interest for structured study and prefer a less structured, exploratory approach. They are currently focusing on blending traditional musical roots with modern sounds and developing an app to help others do the same, and they find fulfillment in creating music that connects to their heritage and personal identity.\",\"t2\":\"The user initially enjoyed discovering new melodies and exploring different genres, but lost interest when diving into technical aspects like music theory (2018) and audio production, finding them stressful and chore-like. They also found researching historical music trends (2020) tedious and overwhelming. They disliked a music documentary for skimming over artistic depth. However, they found fulfillment in attending live festivals (2017 electronic music festival), exploring genres and cultural significance, discovering album artwork/lyrics/stories, creating playlists, and most importantly, creating their own music tracks, which brings joy and a deep emotional connection.\"},\"grounded_subquestion_parts\":[\"How can I find a more fulfilling way to express my love for music?\\nEstablished music_history: \",{\"text_ref\":\"t0\"},\"\\nEstablished current_prefs: \",{\"text_ref\":\"t1\"},\"\\nEstablished attitude_changes: \",{\"text_ref\":\"t2\"}]}"}], "logical_call_index": 12, "response_format": "plain", "input_tokens_local": 11170, "output_token_reserve": 4096, "input_margin": 256, "max_model_len": 120000, "tokenization_request_sha256": "bed97743a0ae2859a81a392e459e7543e7bdde8f8b5e082e915863db8b360fbd", "tokenization_endpoint_sha256": "0ed12ee94b55bfdbc62fb247243af2d71aa1d7ea503f5f191605ae295c5ad94a", "token_count_is_estimate": false, "token_estimator_id": "deployment_vllm_chat_v1", "tokenizer_id": null, "add_generation_prompt": true, "tokenization_scope": "adapted_plain_text_chat_default_server_template", "token_accounting_note": "Deployment input count; model weights and tokenizer hash are not independently verified", "tokenization_wire_sha256": "ea37d9987d359efb49b29702e483b48891610ced8372a2ae6f92e936a72b8a0a", "raw_output": "{\n  \"slots\": [\n    {\n      \"variable\": \"music_history\",\n      \"observations\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fact_9b863bf250c7624bc715353e\",\n          \"stance\": \"support\",\n          \"value\": \"The user has explored various genres and attended festivals, including an electronic music festival in 2017. They tried music theory classes in 2018 but found it unfulfilling, preferring emotional connection over technic