ected to their heritage and personal identity.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"variable\": \"attitude_changes\",\n      \"observations\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fact_ec925d62ef95370d95266352\",\n          \"stance\": \"support\",\n          \"value\": \"The user initially enjoyed discovering new melodies and exploring different genres, but lost interest when diving into technical aspects like music theory (2018) and audio production, finding them stressful and chore-like. They also found researching historical music trends (2020) tedious and overwhelming. They disliked a music documentary for skimming over artistic depth. However, they found fulfillment in attending live festivals (2017 electronic music festival), exploring genres and cultural significance, discovering album artwork/lyrics/stories, creating playlists, and most importantly, creating their own music tracks, which brings joy and a deep emotional connection.\",\n          \"source_ids\": [\"s22\",\"s23\",\"s11\",\"s12\",\"s31\",\"s46\",\"s13\",\"s4\",\"s3\",\"s33\",\"s47\",\"s32\",\"s14\",\"s10\",\"s35\",\"s43\",\"s34\",\"s45\",\"s44\"],\n          \"entity_scope\": \"user\",\n          \"time_scope\": \"past\",\n          \"parent_versions\": {},\n          \"retract_ids\": [],\n          \"reason\": \"The user explicitly describes past enjoyment of discovery and festivals, followed by loss of interest in theory, production, and historical research, and a shift toward emotional engagement and personal creation. All cited sources are user statements from the provided conversation history.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"variable\": \"response\",\n      \"observations\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"obs_response_1\",\n          \"stance\": \"support\",\n          \"value\": \"Collaborating with others who share your musical interests can also be a rewarding path. A user found fulfillment through working with